# Ansel Fenn: comic, then not, then comic.
dialogue ansel
  # Chained straight on from the kiss (pike at turn); the hotspot opens at `taller`.
  node across narrator "He crosses the salt pan before I move. He stops a yard away. He doesn't touch me."
    -> paperwork
  node paperwork narrator "I had three years to think what to say. All I thought of was paperwork."
    -> taller
  node taller ansel "You're taller. Is that regulation?"
    > "Hello, Father." -> hello
      add aff 1
    > "You left the compass on the hall table." -> table
  node hello ansel "Hello, son."
    -> look
  node table ansel "I did. On purpose. Cray wanted it. I thought: my son has a desk and a stamp. He can't get into trouble."
    -> look
  node look narrator "He looks at me properly. The salt. The stamp. The pirate beside me."
    -> sorry
  node sorry ansel "…Look at you. I'm sorry about the beard. And your shirts. Most of them are flags now. I'm sorry about the beard."
    -> years
  node years ansel "And the three years. I should have said that first."
    > "They wrote you down as lost. I believed it." -> neat
  node neat ansel "(gently) Well. It was very neat handwriting."
    -> flags
  node flags ansel "Fifteen flags. Every morning I thought: someone will look up."
    > "I read the log. The L is for her." if log_read -> lise
    > "What's the L for?" if not log_read -> whatl
    > "Your sewing is terrible." -> sewing
  node lise ansel "She always said I couldn't sew. Fifteen flags, and she's still right. I think she'd have liked that best."
    -> you
  node whatl ansel "Lise. Your mother. She always said I couldn't sew. Fifteen flags, and she's still right."
    -> you
  node sewing ansel "Your mother said that. In that exact voice. Fifteen flags, and I still haven't proved her wrong. Don't tell her. Well. You know."
    -> you
  node you ansel "And you are?"
    -> nav
  node nav quill "The navigator."
    -> course
  node course ansel "(delighted) Of course you are."
    -> log
  node log ansel "I'd say I didn't see anything. But I'm a captain. We see everything. We just log it later."
    -> dare
  node dare quill "Don't you dare log it."
    -> loft
  node loft ansel "His mother kissed me in a sail loft. I'd just been fined."
    -> what
  node what quill "What for?"
    -> being
  node being ansel "Being in a sail loft."
    -> crews
  node crews ansel "Pike says everyone's been inspected. A hundred and thirty sailors. The Weather took every boat. I'm not leaving without them."
    > "A ship waits outside the Needle. It needs a flag." -> sixteen
      give flag16
      set ansel_met
      sound pickup
    > "A ship brought me. You won't have to stay." -> sixteen
      give flag16
      set ansel_met
      sound pickup
  node sixteen ansel "Then she wants sixteen. I was putting it up this morning. Here. L in the corner. She checks."
    -> colour
  node colour ansel "She'd have hated the colour. It's mustard. On purpose."
    > "Why mustard?" -> why
      add aff 1
    > "I'll run it up." -> run
  node why ansel "So she'd come back to complain. It hasn't worked yet. I'm a patient sewer. Sewist. Man with a needle."
    -> run
  node run ansel "The halyard's on the mainmast. Follow the stakes, not me. I go wrong at the third one. I'll bring the lads to the beach."
  # Afterwards.
  node hub ansel "Still here? The flag won't raise itself. I've asked it. Nicely, and then not."
    > "What did the Weather do with you?" -> receipt
    > "Rook's alive. He's in Port Vela." if met_rook and not seen:ansel.rook -> rook
    > "I read the last page." if has ansel_log and not seen:ansel.page -> page
    > "I still have the desk. At the customs house." if not seen:ansel.desk -> desk
    > "Why keep raising flags?" -> why2
    > "Where do you go, when you want to think?" if not seen:pans.root -> barrel
    > "I'm going." -> go
  node receipt ansel "Polite men. They gave every one of us a receipt for himself. I've still got mine. “One captain, used.” I'd argue with “used”."
  node rook ansel "Rook! They said he was dead. (He stops.) Is he well?"
    -> drunk
  node drunk ansel "Don't answer that. Is he drunk?"
    > "Very." -> well
    > "He's been waiting for you. In a tavern." -> well
      add aff 1
  node well ansel "Then he's well. Good. I'll want my navigator back. He owes me a reef."
  node page ansel "(He goes pink under the sunburn.) You weren't meant to read that. I'm glad you did. Keep it."
  node desk ansel "A desk is a fine thing. So is a deck. Only one letter between them."
    -> desk2
  node desk2 ansel "I'm not saying which way to spell it. I'm your father, not your Harbourmaster."
  node why2 ansel "Every time they tore one down, somebody had to write it down. I like to think I ruined a lot of afternoons."
  # The far pans (far_pans.adv): optional.
  node barrel ansel "The far pans. I've a barrel down there with a view of the old girl. Come on. I'll show you."
    go far_pans sound none
  node go ansel "Go on, then. Follow the stakes. Not me. Never me."
